# nr-office-engine-digest: the model-facing result digest (finalizeOfficeResult, officeDocumentDigest, bounded, stableJson) of crate mixdog-office.

The code is in native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/digest/{mod,common,docx,xlsx,pptx,pdf,tabular}.rs and
native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/bounded.rs. It was not compiled by this task (no cargo run): the three edits below
to files this task does not own are needed before it can be.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod capabilities;` add (and extend the crate doc by one line saying `digest` is what a model reads of a result and
`bounded` its length-bounded form):

    pub mod bounded;
    pub mod digest;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml

[dependencies]: add, after `indexmap`:

    mixdog-js = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies]: add (the helpers of the twin tests, as mixdog-office-base's own manifest describes):

    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }

(mixdog-js and mixdog-office-base are already [workspace.dependencies] and workspace members. `serde_json` already has
`preserve_order` workspace-wide, which the digest relies on for Node's key order.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package `mixdog-office`: add the dependencies `mixdog-js` and `mixdog-office-base` (both already packages of the lock; nothing
else changes: `cargo update -w` offline).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Nothing to add by hand: no new external crate and no new feature (serde_json, mixdog-js and mixdog-office-base's own
dependencies are already unified). Run the hakari check after the manifest edit and take its output if it asks for a line.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index of the fixture sets)

Add this entry right after the `office-detect` entry (the list is sorted by `set`):

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-digest.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-digest/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "da8c326cbb3abf80c0182e723169f8c9a9e3cff034387a05dce6ba0fb5e0d36a",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-digest.mjs",
      "set": "office-digest",
      "totalBytes": 127712
    },

(The set was recorded from the product tree at C:/Project/mixdog, which is not an exact commit export, so its manifest
`product.commit` is null. A re-record from the exact archive tree the other office sets use changes the manifest and its
sha256 in this entry; the golden's cases do not depend on it.)

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.

## Later tasks

- The session layer (office-sessions port) fills `digest::ResultSession` from its session (`target`, `format`, `file_kind`,
  `authored`, `facts_mode_sample` from `authoredBrief.factsMode === 'sample'`) and keeps `delivered_design` /
  `delivered_model_review` on the stored session between results; it calls `finalize_office_result(copy_of_value,
  FinalizeOptions { action, session, elapsed_ms })` with `elapsed_ms` = `performance.now() - startedAt`, and
  `bounded::bounded(&value, max_chars, Some(model_facing_length))`, where `modelFacingLength` is the UTF-16 length of the
  serialisation of the value with `digest::office_document_digest` applied to its `document` (office-sessions.mjs).
- `digest::FACTS_SAMPLE_DISCLOSURE` is the text of `FACTS_SAMPLE_DISCLOSURE` in authoring/pptx-brief.mjs; the authoring port
  reuses the constant rather than writing it again.
